Chapter: DeskLabelMetricsTest
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Works chapter GopFont
  cites Works chapter GopDraw
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopComposite
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 `widget-label` and `widget-button` reserve `text-length * 8` logical pixels,
 an EIGHT PIXEL CELL hardcoded in `Widget.codex`, and the renderer then draws
 a proportional face. This prints the two numbers side by side so the gap is a
 table rather than an adjective, then prints the same table for the tree
 `comp-fit-text` has re-measured through the loaded face: the second table's
 slack is what the desk actually reserves now, and it is the rounding of one
 device pixel per string rather than tens.

 Measured 2026-08-21 with CMUNSS at 1600 wide over the sidebar, and it
 answered in BOTH directions: the four lowercase buttons reserved 49 to 72
 device pixels MORE than they drew, and `CODEX` reserved 80 against 106 drawn,
 short by 26. Capitals are wider than the cell and lowercase is narrower, so
 the error is not a margin to be tuned but a per-string measurement that is
 missing.

 RE-MEASURED 2026-08-25 over the taskbar, the sidebar having been deleted:
 the menu entry reserves 256 device pixels against 93 drawn, and 126 against
 93 once `comp-fit-text` has re-measured it through the face. The direction
 and the size of the correction both survive the change of specimen; the
 two-directions half does not, because one string cannot show two directions,
 and that is what the smaller specimen costs.

 The under-reservation does no visible harm TODAY only because `flex-col-place`
 gives every child the container's full width, so the brand label is handed 320
 pixels rather than the 80 it asked for. That coupling is the finding: a width
 constraint that stops the full-bleed stretch will start clipping the labels
 the stretch is currently hiding. The cell has to be fixed FIRST.

 It walks the desk's OWN tree rather than a copy of its strings. A label
 listed here would measure this chapter; the tree measured here is the thing
 that ships.

 THE SPECIMEN IS THE TASKBAR, AND THE START MENU CANNOT BE ONE. The sidebar
 was the specimen until it was deleted, and the obvious replacement is the
 menu, which carries the longest run of labels the desk has. Measured, every
 row of it reserves ZERO: `gpr-row` and the Shutdown row are built with
 `widget-set-min ... 0 22`, which sets the width minimum to nothing and lets
 the column stretch, so the eight-pixel cell is never consulted and the whole
 menu measures to 40 against the 520 it is drawn at. A tree that never asks
 the cell for a width cannot measure the cell.

 The taskbar does ask: `desk-taskbar` sets its entry to `mb.wn-min-w`, the
 button's OWN natural reservation, which is exactly the number under test.
 That it is a shorter table than the sidebar gave is the honest cost of the
 sidebar going, and the alternative was a table of zeroes that still looked
 like a measurement.

 WHAT A GATED RUN PROVES IS NOT THE METRIC. `seed/Codex.img` carries no
 typeface and the battery attaches no disk, so the recorded answer is the
 no-volume line: it proves this chapter still compiles against `GopDesk` and
 `GopFont` and that the mount is reached, and NOTHING about type. The table
 with a face lives in `ShellRefinement.md` beside the command that rebuilds
 it, which needs an image from `build-boot-img.ps1` (L-NAMED, and the same
 shape as `desk-leading-metrics`).

Section: Body

  dlm-w : Integer = 1600

  label-of : WidgetNode -> Text
  label-of (n) = when n.wn-kind
    is WkLabel (t) -> t
    is WkButton (t) -> t
    is otherwise -> ""

  pad : Text, Integer -> Text
  pad (t) (n) = if text-length t >= n then t else pad (t & " ") n

  row : WidgetNode, GopFont, Integer -> Text
  row (n) (tf) (s) =
    let t = label-of n
    in let reserved = n.wn-min-w * s
    in let drawn = gfont-text-w tf t
    in pad (n.wn-id) 10 & pad ("chars " & integer-to-text (text-length t)) 10
       & pad ("reserved " & integer-to-text reserved) 15
       & pad ("drawn " & integer-to-text drawn) 12
       & "slack " & integer-to-text (reserved - drawn)

  min-of : WidgetNode, Text -> Integer
  min-of (root) (id) = when widget-find root id
    is Just (n) -> n.wn-min-w
    is None -> 0 - 1

 The rows are a panel down from the menu's root, and `walk` goes one level, so
 the column is fetched by id rather than reached by descent. `gpr-menu` holds
 both the group headings and the open group's app rows, which are the two
 shapes the eight-pixel cell gets wrong in opposite directions.

  kids-of : WidgetNode, Text -> List WidgetNode
  kids-of (root) (id) = when widget-find root id
    is Just (n) -> n.wn-children
    is None -> []

  count-of : WidgetNode, Text -> Integer
  count-of (root) (id) = when widget-find root id
    is Just (n) -> n.wn-child-count
    is None -> 0

  walk : List WidgetNode, Integer, Integer, GopFont, Integer -> [Console] Integer
  walk (kids) (i) (n) (tf) (s) =
    if i >= n then 0
    else let k = list-at kids i
    in if text-length (label-of k) == 0 then walk kids (i + 1) n tf s
    else act
      r <- print-line-uni (row k tf s)
      walk kids (i + 1) n tf s
    end

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    m <- gfat-mount-esp
    if m.gm-ok == False then print-line-uni "no FAT volume on the boot medium"
    else act
      let ppem = dk-ui-ppem dlm-w
      in let s = ui-wscale dlm-w
      in act
        f <- gfont-load (m.gm-vol) "CMUNSS.TTF" ppem
        if f.gf-ok == False then print-line-uni "CMUNSS.TTF: not loaded"
        else act
          let th = dk-theme-of 0 dk-adorn-default
          in let ds = alloc-zeroed 256 64
          in let ps = alloc-zeroed 64 64
          in let bar = widget-measure (desk-taskbar ds gfont-none s) th
          in let fit = widget-measure (comp-fit-text (desk-taskbar ds f s) f s) th
          in act
            print-line-uni ("clock pinned to       : " & integer-to-text (desk-task-clock-w * s))
            w <- walk (bar.wn-children) 0 (bar.wn-child-count) f s
            print-line-uni ("taskbar measured to   : " & integer-to-text (bar.wn-min-w * s))
            print-line-uni "fitted through the face:"
            w2 <- walk (fit.wn-children) 0 (fit.wn-child-count) f s
            print-line-uni ("fitted measured to    : " & integer-to-text (fit.wn-min-w * s))
            print-line-uni ("a menu row reserves   : " & integer-to-text (min-of (widget-measure (gpr-menu-tree ps) th) "gpr-Clock"))
            let tb = comp-fit-text (desk-taskbar 0 f s) f s
            in act
              print-line-uni ("fitted menu button    : " & integer-to-text (min-of tb "menu"))
              print-line-uni ("pinned clock 220      : " & integer-to-text (min-of tb "task-clock"))
            end
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end

